<article class="env-lemma" id="00XS">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/00XS">Lemma <span data-tag="00XS">7.21.6</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{C}$ and $\mathcal{D}$ be sites. Let $u : \mathcal{C} \to \mathcal{D}$ be a functor. Assume that </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li class="custom-item" data-marker="(a)"><p>
$u$ is cocontinuous, 
</p>
</li><li class="custom-item" data-marker="(b)"><p>
$u$ is continuous, and 
</p>
</li><li class="custom-item" data-marker="(c)"><p>
fibre products and equalizers exist in $\mathcal{C}$ and $u$ commutes with them. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> In this case the functor $g_!$ above commutes with fibre products and equalizers (and more generally with finite connected limits). </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Assume (a), (b), and (c). We have $g_! = (u_ p\  )^\# $. Recall (Lemma <a href="/tag/00W2" data-tag="00W2">7.10.1</a>) that limits of sheaves are equal to the corresponding limits as presheaves. And sheafification commutes with finite limits (Lemma <a href="/tag/00WJ" data-tag="00WJ">7.10.15</a>). Thus it suffices to show that $u_ p$ commutes with fibre products and equalizers. To do this it suffices that colimits over the categories $(\mathcal{I}_ V^ u)^{opp}$ of Section <a href="/tag/00VC" data-tag="00VC">7.5</a> commute with fibre products and equalizers. This follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/00X4" data-tag="00X4">7.5.1</a> and Categories, Lemma <a href="/tag/002Y" data-tag="002Y">4.19.9</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>